__pycache__/
docs/_build/*
docs/_autosummary/*

.DS_STORE

# editor / agent tooling state (never part of the package)
.claude/

# local docs build environment
.venv-docs/

# build artifacts
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
*.so
# Cython-generated C source (regenerated at build time)
rainbow/agilent/_uvdelta.c
rainbow/agilent/_msprofile.c
rainbow/agilent/_chdelta.c

# working notes, not part of the package
/asm-notes/
/asm-reference/

# Local datasets and anything derived from them. Keep them here rather than
# adding a new entry per dataset: a per-dataset line is a poor guard, since it
# protects only what someone remembered to list, and the entry outlives the
# data.
/data/
/datasets/
# exported ASM documents (never commit; these come from real samples)
/ASMs/

# Every directory at the repository root is ignored unless it is named below.
# A dataset is always a directory (a .D, a .raw, a .dx bundle, a folder of
# them), so this covers one left at the root whatever it is called, and it is
# never one `git add -A` away from being committed. Listing the datasets by
# name instead would only ever cover the ones somebody thought to add.
#
# Only directories, deliberately. Ignoring root *files* too would mean a new
# CONTRIBUTING.md or .pre-commit-config.yaml is invisible to `git status` and
# `git add -A`, and silently deleted by `git clean -fdx`. Losing an uncommitted
# file that way is worse than the thing being prevented, since committing a
# dataset is at least loud and revertible. The single-file archive formats are
# named individually just below.
#
# The cost that remains: a genuinely new project *directory* at the root is
# ignored, so add it here when you add it. Everything inside the directories
# below behaves normally.
/*/
/*.dx
/*.zip
/*.asm.json
!/.github/
!/docs/
!/rainbow/
!/scripts/
!/tests/
